parts[0]='The inhabitants of Mesopotamia – which now forms part of eastern Syria, southeastern Turkey and Iraq – lived for thousands of years on individual farms and in small, isolated communities, working relentlessly just to meet their basic needs. But then, about 6,000 years ago something remarkable happened. The people left the security of their family homes and villages and came together with others to create something far more complex and difficult: the world’s first city, called Uruk.'
